    (0, None, '\'Max, we need to talk seriously!\' "To us it\'s necessary" is a casual way to say "we must". The word is a cousin of the "needed" one. Vika has had enough waiting, and she says so.'),
    (1, None, '\'Hey, Vika! Glad to see you.\' "Privet" is the casual hello. "Glad" ends bare, because Max is a man. His smile is as false as the greeting. It\'s the reaction of a man who has seen the boss\'s niece coming.'),
    (2, None, '\'Oh, Kostya is calling, sorry!\' In Russian, "rings" is the one used for the phone. And "sorry" is the casual command from the first scene, "excuse me". Max waves his phone as he says it.'),
