    (4, None, '\'Hard to hear, I will come over right now!\' "Badly audible" is what Russians say for "I can hardly hear". "Come over" is the same walking-up word as before. Max takes a step toward the door as he speaks.'),
    (5, None, '\'Max, wait, do not leave!\' The "away" in "do not go away" is the little u- on the front. Its opposite is the pri- of "come", and you can hear them in "uhodit" and "prihodit". Vika isn\'t fooled.'),
